*> Implementation test (002-lane-mobs3, T4220; docs/protocol/34-9 section 14 experience orb, 34-6 creeper scale, 20 section 6.1 creeper metadata 16, 21
*> section 8.2 orb metadata 8): the client keeps the value of an orb (Set Entity Data entry 8, INT) and the swell direction of a creeper (entry 16, INT:
*> -1 idle, 1 fusing). An orb is drawn as one camera-facing quad (6 vertices) 0.3 wide from y + 0.025 to y + 0.325 on the icon of its value
*> (value 20: icon 3, u from 0.75 to 1.0 of the 16-wide icon sheet of 64 x 64); the creeper's swell counter runs 1 a tick (50 ms) while the direction is 1
*> and its model scales by 1 + c^4 x 0.4 in x and z (c = swell / 28): after 14 ticks (c = 0.5) about 1.0237.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-ORB-SWELL.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CLMODELS.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ORB-ID              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CREEPER-ID          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW-AREA            PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-INDEX               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FIRST               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LAST                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RANGE.
    05 WS-R                BINARY-LONG OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 01 WS-WIDTH-IDLE          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WIDTH-SWELL         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-U-EXPECT            FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HIT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ARROW-ID            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-EDIT-A              PIC -(6)9.
 01 WS-EDIT-B              PIC -(6)9.
 01 WS-YAW-SET             FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 WS-PITCH-SET           FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-EYE-TABLE.
    05 WS-EYE              FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 3 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 0 TO PK-COUNT
     CALL "ENTITY-ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 256 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO SK-U PL-YAW
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EYE(1) WS-EYE(3)
     MOVE 64 TO WS-EYE(2)
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "experience_orb" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ORB-ID WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "creeper" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-CREEPER-ID WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
*>   An orb of value 20.
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-X
     MOVE 64 TO WS-Y
     MOVE 12.5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "EOS-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-ORB-ID WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     MOVE 8 TO WS-INDEX
     MOVE 20 TO WS-VALUE
     CALL "EOS-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-INDEX WS-VALUE
     MOVE "entity orb the value of Set Entity Data entry 8 is kept" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 20 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-VALUE(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE "entity orb is one quad of 6 vertices" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Its height: y + 0.025 to y + 0.325 above the eye (64 - 64 = 0): 25 to 325 thousandths; its width 0.3 across the camera's right.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE 6 TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE "entity orb spans y + 0.025 to y + 0.325" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 325 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-R(4) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "entity orb bottom edge y + 0.025" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 25 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-R(3) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   The icon: some vertex has u = (slot x + 0.75 w) / atlas w and another (slot x + 1.0 w) / atlas w (icon 3 is the fourth of the row).
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HIT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 6
         COMPUTE WS-U-EXPECT = (EA-MT-X(1) + 0.75 * EA-MT-W(1)) / EA-W
         IF RL-EN-U(WS-I) > WS-U-EXPECT - 0.0001 AND RL-EN-U(WS-I) < WS-U-EXPECT + 0.0001
             ADD 1 TO WS-HIT
         END-IF
         COMPUTE WS-U-EXPECT = (EA-MT-X(1) + 1.0 * EA-MT-W(1)) / EA-W
         IF RL-EN-U(WS-I) > WS-U-EXPECT - 0.0001 AND RL-EN-U(WS-I) < WS-U-EXPECT + 0.0001
             ADD 10 TO WS-HIT
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "entity orb value 20 uses icon 3 (u 0.75 to 1.0): 3 + 3 vertices of the two triangles" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 33 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-HIT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A creeper: idle, then fusing for 14 ticks.
     CALL "ENTITIES-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 6 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 20.5 TO WS-X
     MOVE 20.5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "EOS-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-CREEPER-ID WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     MOVE 1000000 TO CL-NOW-MS
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     COMPUTE WS-WIDTH-IDLE = WS-R(2) - WS-R(1)
     MOVE 16 TO WS-INDEX
     MOVE 1 TO WS-VALUE
     CALL "EOS-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-INDEX WS-VALUE
     MOVE "entity creeper the swell direction of entry 16 is kept" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-SWELL-DIR(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     COMPUTE CL-NOW-MS = 1000000 + 700
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     COMPUTE WS-WIDTH-SWELL = WS-R(2) - WS-R(1)
*>   The ratio in thousandths: 1.0237 expected, within 1.018 to 1.030.
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-WIDTH-SWELL * 1000 / WS-WIDTH-IDLE
     MOVE "entity creeper after 14 fusing ticks is 1.024 times as wide (1 + c^4 x 0.4, c = 0.5)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HIT
     IF TL-OBSERVED-N >= 1018 AND TL-OBSERVED-N <= 1030
         MOVE 1 TO WS-HIT
     END-IF
     MOVE WS-HIT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   An arrow (34-9 section 4): six quads (two crossing shaft planes and the fletching plane, both sides each); the tip points along the flight direction:
*>   at yaw 0 pitch 0 the shaft (nock x = -12, tip x = 4 pixels, scale 0.9 / 16) lies along +z from the entity, at yaw 90 along +x.
     CALL "ENTITIES-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "arrow" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ARROW-ID WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE 7 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-X
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "EOS-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-ARROW-ID WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE "entity arrow is 6 quads of 6 vertices" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 36 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE "entity arrow at yaw 0 flies along +z: the tip 0.225 and the nock 0.675 from the entity" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "-175 725" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-R(5) TO WS-EDIT-A
     MOVE WS-R(6) TO WS-EDIT-B
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT-A) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT-B) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 90 TO WS-YAW-SET
     CALL "EOS-ROTATE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-YAW-SET WS-PITCH-SET
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "entity arrow at yaw 90 flies along +x" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "-175 725" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-R(1) TO WS-EDIT-A
     MOVE WS-R(2) TO WS-EDIT-B
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT-A) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT-B) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
*>   Pitch 45 degrees (rising): the tip is above the nock by 16 x 0.05625 x sin 45 = 0.64: the highest vertex is the tip's.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-YAW-SET
     MOVE 45 TO WS-PITCH-SET
     CALL "EOS-ROTATE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-YAW-SET WS-PITCH-SET
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FIRST
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO WS-LAST
     CALL "ETM-RANGE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-FIRST WS-LAST WS-RANGE
     MOVE "entity arrow rising at pitch 45 spans 0.64 + the planes' height up (above 0.6 and under 0.8)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-R(4) - WS-R(3) > 600 AND WS-R(4) - WS-R(3) < 800
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The vertex capacity (CL-MAX-ENTITY-VERTICES): an arrow (36 vertices) or an orb (6) that would not fit is not emitted.
     CALL "ENTITY-MODEL-SLOTS" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE RL-EN-COUNT = CL-MAX-ENTITY-VERTICES - 30
     MOVE 1 TO WS-ONE
     CALL "ENTITY-ARROW-EMIT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ONE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE "entity arrow with less room than its 36 vertices is not emitted" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = CL-MAX-ENTITY-VERTICES - 30
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITIES-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ID
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-X
     MOVE 64 TO WS-Y
     MOVE 12.5 TO WS-Z
     CALL "EOS-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-ORB-ID WS-X WS-Y WS-Z
     CALL "ENTITY-MODEL-SLOTS" USING CLIENT-STATE
     COMPUTE RL-EN-COUNT = CL-MAX-ENTITY-VERTICES - 3
     CALL "ENTITY-ORB-EMIT" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ONE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE "entity orb with less room than its 6 vertices is not emitted" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = CL-MAX-ENTITY-VERTICES - 3
     MOVE RL-EN-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-ORB-SWELL.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EOS-ROTATE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, yaw, pitch (FLOAT-SHORT): the replica row's angles (what Move Entity Pos Rot leaves there).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-YAW                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 01 L-PITCH                FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-YAW L-PITCH.
     CALL "ENTITY-FIND" USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID WS-ROW
     MOVE L-YAW TO EN-YAW(WS-ROW) EN-HEAD-YAW(WS-ROW)
     MOVE L-PITCH TO EN-PITCH(WS-ROW)
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EOS-ROTATE.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EOS-SPAWN.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, type (registry id), x y z (FLOAT-LONG): Add Entity at rest.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-ADD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-V0                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V1                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V2                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-A0                  FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    FLOAT-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-TYPE L-X L-Y L-Z.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER WS-V0 WS-V1 WS-V2
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-ADD
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EOS-SPAWN.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. EOS-DATA.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, entry index, INT value: Set Entity Data with one INT entry.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==MD-==.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-DATA                BINARY-LONG VALUE 101.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-INDEX                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-VALUE                BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-INDEX L-VALUE.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     INITIALIZE MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE L-INDEX TO MD-MD-INDEX
     MOVE MD-MDS-INT TO MD-MD-SERIALIZER
     MOVE L-VALUE TO MD-MD-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE MD-MD-END TO MD-MD-INDEX
     CALL "PB-PUT-ENTITY-METADATA" USING PB-BUFFER MD-METADATA-ENTRY
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-DATA
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM EOS-DATA.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ETM-RANGE.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, first and last entity vertex, range out (BINARY-LONG x 6): min and max x, y, z in thousandths.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-V                   BINARY-LONG.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-FIRST                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-LAST                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-RANGE.
    05 L-R                 BINARY-LONG OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-FIRST L-LAST L-RANGE.
     MOVE 999999999 TO L-R(1) L-R(3) L-R(5)
     MOVE -999999999 TO L-R(2) L-R(4) L-R(6)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM L-FIRST BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > L-LAST
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-X(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(1), WS-V) TO L-R(1)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(2), WS-V) TO L-R(2)
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-Y(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(3), WS-V) TO L-R(3)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(4), WS-V) TO L-R(4)
         COMPUTE WS-V = FUNCTION INTEGER(RL-EN-Z(WS-I) * 1000 + 0.5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(L-R(5), WS-V) TO L-R(5)
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(L-R(6), WS-V) TO L-R(6)
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM ETM-RANGE.
 COPY CLTEST.
